  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1958\n£5.00\n\n6 available\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1958 quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nCompiled and Edited by Brigadier-General C. G. Higgins, C.M.G., D.S.O., D.L. Volume LX January to December 1958.\n\nPublished 1959 - Sydney Lee (Exeter) Ltd. Hardcover.\n\n \n\nContents:\n\nThe Army List September 1958 -p.1\n\nExtracts from the 'London Gazette' -p.3\n\nRegular Officers of the Regiment Extra-Regimentally Employed -p.6\n\nFormer Officers of the Regiment on the Active List -p.7\n\nReorganisation of the Green Jackets Brigade -p.8\n\nLetters and Messages Exchanged on Leaving the Infantry Brigade -p.9\n\nInaugration Parade of the New Green Jackets Brigade -p.11\n\nRecords of the 1st Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd -p.12\n\nSummary of the 1st Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd Diary -p.15\n\nFirst Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd Letter -p.27\n\nPolo -p.34\n\nTown Company -p.35\n\nFirst Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd, Records of Sport and Training 1958 -p.39\n\nRecords of Regimental Headquarters -p.46\n\nRegimental Headquarters Letter -p.47\n\nRegimental Cricket Week -49\n\nRecords of the Fourth Battalion -p.55\n\nFourth Battalion Letter -p.58\n\nRegimental Dinner -p.64\n\n52nd Light Infantry Luncheon (First World War) -p.65\n\n43rd Light Infantry Dinner (Second World War) -p.66\n\n52nd Light Infantry Dinner(Second World War) -p.67\n\n43rd Light Infantry (Mesopotamia) Luncheon -p.68\n\nThe Wolfe Society Dinner -p.69\n\nFishmongers' Company Livery Dinner -p.70\n\nI Write As I Please -p.71\n\nOn Safari -p.82\n\nOld Soldiers and Guardians of the Queen's Peace -p.86\n\nNorth American Holiday  -p.98\n\nOld Comrades' Association 1957 -p.105\n\nMarriage -p. 106\n\nObituary -p.107\n\nIndex -p.109\n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nRemembered: The Men on the War Memorials of Witney, Crawley and Hailey. Volume 2: 1939-1945.\n£9.99 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre I\n£5.00 Add to cart\nIdentifying Cap Badges: A Family Historian’s Guide\n£25.00 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre V\n£5.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
